/// Process control for Miri.
///
/// Provides functions to terminate the process with an exit code.

runtime "core" fn miri_rt_exit(code int)

/// Terminates the program with the given exit code.
///
/// This function does not return; the process exits immediately after flushing
/// output. Destructors do not run, so a value still live at the call site is not
/// released. A shell observes only the low 8 bits of the code, per POSIX.
///
/// This is a free function rather than a capability method because the call never
/// returns, so a capability handle would gate nothing — the same reasoning that
/// leaves `panic()` a free function.
///
/// Example:
///     if args.length() == 0
///         println("usage: prog <args>")
///         exit(1)
public fn exit(code int)
    miri_rt_exit(code)
